Subject: [PATCH 03314/11362] [outer-loop] arc: pretrained mechanic prior
 TRANSFERS to unseen games (5/5) -- result + note

The keystone validation of the capture/pretrain reframe: a cross-game dynamics prior trained on 20 public
games transfers to 5 held-out games it never saw. Warm-started learner reaches 28-47% changed-cell accuracy
from 60 transitions where from-scratch gets ~0 -- mean cell-recall scratch 0.034 -> warm 0.314 (~9x), warm
wins 5/5. This is the mechanism the hidden eval needs (a prior -> faster live adaptation -> fewer real
probes -> more 5n budget to solve).

results/arc_pretrain_prior.json (the validated transfer result, verifier_is_oracle=false) +
docs/research-notes/arc-pretrain-prior-transfers-2026-06-21.md (result table + the 4-iteration debugging
arc: full-grid 0/5 -> residual 0/5 -> identity-collapse diagnosis -> change-weighted-loss fix -> 5/5; the
honest caveats: exact-match still 0 / cell-recall is the signal, CPU-bound, representation headroom; and
the next levers: GPU, object-delta + TRM representations, wire prior_state into the live agent).

